      "text_raw": "Take as an example, this\nlow-pass filter. The low-fre-\nquency gain A is a ratio of\nv0\nresistors, which can be made\nquite accurately.\nThe cut-off frequency\nf however depends on a\n−3dB\nproduct of a resistor R and\n2\nthe capacitor C. There is no\nway that this product R C\n2\ncan be realized in an accu-\nrate way. Errors of more\nthan 20% cannot be\navoided.\nSubstitution of this resis-\ntor R by its switched-\n2\ncapacitor equivalent, will involve ratios only, which are easily realized with great accuracy.",
      "text": "Take as an example, this low-pass filter. The low-frequency gain A is a ratio of v0 resistors, which can be made quite accurately. The cut-off frequency f however depends on a −3dB product of a resistor R and 2 the capacitor C. There is no way that this product R C 2 can be realized in an accurate way. Errors of more than 20% cannot be avoided. Substitution of this resistor R by its switched- 2 capacitor equivalent, will involve ratios only, which are easily realized with great accuracy."
